member.summary:
Every second (real time): closes a drama dialog left open for 5 s (NPC/stalker joining a battle, an opponent
escaping...). A drama pauses the game timers, so OnTimeUpdate100ms (the step runner) would never run again;
the 5 s let the scenarios that open a drama check it first.

Local stand-in of the BugSplat upload API for TT-06 (127.0.0.1, free port, a background thread): answers the 3
requests of CrashReportHelper like BugSplat and S3 do and records every request (the evidence of what a player's
game would send). Used through CrashReportHelper.ServerUrlOverride.
  GET  /api/getCrashUploadUrl       -> {"url": "<base>/upload/crash.zip?X-Amz-Signature=autotest"}
  PUT  /upload/crash.zip            -> 200, ETag "<ETAG>"
  POST /api/commitS3CrashUpload     -> {"status": "success", "crashId": 4242}

Registers a CachableObject (ModChild/ModEvent) in ModLib.
CacheId identifies the object and its cache file; OrderIndex sets execution order;
CacheType chooses when it is loaded/saved (Global = title screen, Local = per save game);
WorkOn limits where its events run (All, Global = title screen only, Local = in save game only).

The unit commands of an effect removed (Unit*Ctrl components: UnitCmdCtrl...). A skill gives them their unit;
on an effect created alone they throw (UnitCmdCtrl.TargetUnit) inside the game's TimerMgr, which then stops
every timer of the game for good. A UnityEvent does not call a destroyed component.

A file "*_wallpaper.json" of ModConf: one wallpaper (property names are not case-sensitive):
{ "image": "taoist_1_wallpaper.png", "name": null, "order": 0, "hideGameTitle": true, "startupRate": 0.25,
  "startupWhenChosen": false }

Errors with a known cause the player can fix himself: the exception dialog shows the reason and what to do instead
of the stack trace (the log keeps the stack), and they are not sent as error reports.
Known errors (first found in the exception and its inner exceptions, in this order):
- ModUserException: its message (thrown by a mod, e.g. ConfigMissing);
- FileNotFoundException / DirectoryNotFoundException of a file in the ModConf / ModImg / ModCode folder of a mod:
  the mod folder is incomplete (bad manual install, broken Workshop download);
- a JSON error (Newtonsoft JsonException) inside a ModConfFileException (InConfFile): a broken config file;
- MissingMemberException (MissingMethod / MissingField) / TypeLoadException: of ModLib = ModLib older than the
  mod needs; of another assembly = game version not matching the mods.
The texts have an English fallback: when the ModConf of ModLib itself is missing, its localTexts are not loaded.
